hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"942","We are Bundar, we are Yahya bin Saeed, we are Muhammad bin Abi Adi, we are Abdul Wahhab, meaning Ibn Abdul Majeed, and Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar. On the authority of Awf ibn Abi Jamila, on the authority of Abu Raja’, he said: Samurah ibn Jundub narrated to us, and Bundar narrated to us something similar from the book of Yahya ibn Saeed, he said: Yahya told us, and he read it to us from our book, he said: Awf told us, Abu Raja’ al-Atardi told us, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say to his companions: “Has any of you ever seen a vision so that he can relate it to whomever God wills?” He tells the story, and he said to us one morning: “Two people came to me tonight, and they sent me, and they said to me: Go, go, so we came upon a man.” He was lying down, and behold, another man was standing on top of him with a rock, and behold, he was falling with the rock and reached his head, and the stone here threatened him. So he follows it, takes it, and returns to it until his head is as it was, then he returns to it and does to it as he did the first time.” So he mentioned the hadith in its length, and said: They said: “As for us, we will inform you. As for the man whom you came to, his head was cut off, for he is a man who takes He rejected the Qur’an and neglected the obligatory prayers.” He mentioned the hadith in its length."
